cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use canli-pit-lake, please cite the software and its author."
title: "canli-pit-lake: A point-in-time market data lake with derived availability semantics"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Canli"
    given-names: "Arhan"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arhancanli/canli-pit-lake"
url: "https://canlicapital.com"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - point-in-time data
  - survivorship bias
  - corporate actions
  - look-ahead bias
  - quantitative research infrastructure
abstract: >-
  canli-pit-lake is the point-in-time data layer of the ALPHAC research engine, published
  standalone. Every analytical read requires an explicit as-of instant and returns only records
  available at that instant; quality flags carry per-bit availability lags so a flag derived from
  future bars cannot be seen by a decision at the current bar; corporate actions are filtered on
  when they became knowable rather than on their ex-date; gaps are reported rather than filled;
  and delisted instruments persist so survivorship bias cannot enter.
